WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.500
Open Results and select the recorded historical Bibliography campaign.
No new benchmark is launched during this recording.

00:06.500 --> 00:15.000
Filter to export_bibtex and julia.wall.time.
Choose version_series to compare the nine tagged versions.

00:15.000 --> 00:48.000
The first saved graph is being rendered by Julia and WGLMakie.
This wait is rendering time, not the export benchmark's measured time.

00:48.000 --> 00:53.000
Inspect the last point: the 0.4.0 tag has a median of 15,450 ns.
The curve retains all nine versions and their measured values.

00:53.000 --> 01:00.000
Switch the metric to julia.alloc.bytes.
This compares Julia allocation activity, not live process RAM.

01:00.000 --> 01:07.000
Switch back to time and select distribution.
The graph shows 100 recorded samples per version, 900 in total.

01:07.000 --> 01:18.000
Choose version_delta to compare each later tag with 0.1.0.
These differences are diagnostic: no CI acceptance threshold was configured.
